## 1. Model-agnostic CF (counterfactual) generation contract — DONE (2026-07-31)

> first I need to make a framework for validation over different models, I need to define a contract for cf image generation so it is compatible with any model because I need extensive evaluation over different models.

Goal: one contract so any model (current per_block_attr HDAE, a future SCM-augmented
HDAE from item 2, a frozen-DiffAE baseline) can be scored by the same CC/FC/CF1
pipeline and compared apples-to-apples. (Metric renamed PCF -> CF1 in this pass, per
your instruction — was "PCF score", now "CF1" everywhere: code, CSV columns, filenames.)

What landed, on branch `item1-cf-contract`:
- `CFModelAdapter` interface in `experiments/hdae/counterfactuals/cf_contract.py`:
  `load(config, ckpt, device)` classmethod, `modeled_attrs` metadata, `encode(images,
  attrs_raw, attr_names) -> state`, `intervene(state, attr, direction) -> state`,
  `render(state) -> images`. `state` is an opaque per-adapter dict; `encode` does semantic
  encoding *and* x_T abduction together (resolves the "one call or two" open decision below
  — needed together for HDAE, and DiffAE's `encode_stochastic` wants the same z_sem anyway).
  A small registry (`register_adapter`/`load_adapter`) dispatches on a new `--model-type`
  CLI flag (default `hdae`).
- `HDAEAdapter` (`hdae_adapter.py`): the `AttributeCFGWrapper`/DDIM-abduction/attribute-CFG
