## 4. Decompose CF1 into observed CF1, unobserved CF1, and Aggregated CF1 — DONE (2026-07-31)

> Fourthly, you can decompose CF1 to observed CF1 and unobserved CF1, and Aggregated CF1.

**Resolved by item 1 (2026-07-31):** "CF1" = the former `PCF`, renamed. Not the stale
`counterfactual_consistency`/`factual_flip_success`/`factual_flip_fail` metric in
`run_cf_consistency.py` -> `cf_aggregate.py` (still broken, see AGENDA.md §6).

**Definitions actually landed (your correction to my first draft below — my original
guess had observed=descendants/unobserved=non-descendants; you redefined it the other
way and it's the redefinition that shipped):**
- **observed** = the graph's other conditioning attributes that are *not* descendants of
  the intervened one (currently: the other 3, since the shipped causal graph, item 2, has
  no edges) — the causal graph "observes"/declares their position, so they're expected to
  stay exactly fixed and are scored strictly, no correlational softening.
- **unobserved** = the 36 non-conditioning CelebA attributes, entirely outside the
  declared graph — no causal claim about them; same flip-rate computation the pre-item-2
  `FC` used, just renamed and with the correlational baseline correction **dropped**
  (see below).
- **CC (Counterfactual Consistency) redefined**, per your instruction, to be "intervened
  node and its descendants": pooled success rate over {intervened attribute flips to
  target} union {each causal descendant's classifier prediction matches the SCM's
  (item 2) propagated counterfactual value}. With the shipped edgeless graph this has zero
  descendants for every attribute, so `CC` is numerically identical to item 1's CC —
  confirmed on a real GPU smoke run (every row's `CC` matched exactly across the item-1
  and item-2 code paths).
- You explicitly deferred scoring descendant "success" with a proxy (e.g. any-direction
  flip) until the SCM existed ("first implement the flows... then this part becomes
  trivial") — so this was built on top of a *working, verified* SCM (item 2's
  `verify_scm.py`), not a placeholder.

**Behavior change, stated explicitly (not buried):** the item-1 `FC_raw`/`FC_corr` /
`CF1_raw`/`CF1_corr` split and `compute_baselines_and_weights`/
`correlation_baseline.json` are **removed**, not kept alongside the new split — your
three-metric ask (cf1-observed, cf1-unobserved, cf1-aggregate) reads as replacing the
correlational-adjustment axis with the causal one, and item 2's own text says this item
"replaces" the correlational baseline. `cf1_per_intervention.csv` gained `n_descendants`,
`n_observed_attrs`, `n_unobserved_attrs` columns so `CF1_observed` (currently a 3-attribute
pool) is never silently read as comparable to `CF1_unobserved` (36 attributes) without
seeing the pool sizes.
- `aggregated CF1` = the same macro/micro/weighted/frontier-area pattern item 1 built for
  raw/corr, now computed for observed/unobserved — `cf1_aggregate.csv`'s
  `macro_CF1_observed`, `micro_CF1_observed`, `weighted_CF1_observed`,
  `frontier_area_observed` and the `_unobserved` counterparts.
- Landed inside `run_cf1_eval.py` (extends `evaluate_intervention`/`main`, no new eval
  files) plus the `CFModelAdapter.intervene()` contract extension described in item 2.

Depends on: item 2 — done, in order.


